{
 "name": "float_close",
 "about": "Out of breath, close: the chest heaving (an additive IdleBreathe, fast and big, calming over the take), shoulders riding up and down with it, the head dropped forward toward the other one (`other`, an actor: forehead to forehead is the card's spacing), lips apart, lids half down. The breathing settles, a small smile, and at `look` both eyes go to the lens (`cam`, a point in his own frame). No ground. Ends looking at the lens. Plays `base` (IdleBreathe) under it from the start, so the take has a clip of its own and nothing adds up when it is baked or played alone (base 0 leaves what plays underneath).",
